{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction","id":1403729,"title":"How can you make Chejop Kejak turn Gold Faction?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-20T17:03:07-07:00","id":1403729,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How can you make Chejop Kejak turn Gold Faction?","content":"I think this might be a more epic goal than laying the Neverborn to rest, destroying Oblivion. or talking Malfeas into using his inside voice.<br /> <br /> There is something I find fascinating about the idea of turning one's utmost opposition into an ally, &amp; Exalted is all about epic goals.<br /> <br /> How could PC's possibly reason or otherwise coerce Chejop Kejak into turning pro-Solar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T17:44:53-07:00","id":1403730,"title":"","content":"One thought is that my impression is Chejop Kejak wants to believe he did the right thing. So, maybe convince him that it's compatible to be Gold Faction now and Bronze Faction then? Like, convince him that the Great Curse exists, and that the Usurpation was necessary because of the Great Curse, then end the Great Curse so now Solars are great?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T18:16:38-07:00","id":1403731,"title":"","content":"Aut's idea certainly wouldn't be a bad place to start. I mean a major thing in his 2e writeup was that the Usurpation was justified, so if you could get him on board with the idea that what was done then is not invalidated by allowing Solars to gain power now. The next part would be convincing him that the Solars are necessary for the continued survival of Creation, and then probably work out some system whereby Solars would be able to acquire power and use it to benefit Creation without becoming the most imminent threat to the world that they were percieved as when the Usurpation happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T18:17:04-07:00","id":1403732,"title":"","content":"With him, only way I can think of is a little trick I like to call &quot;Reincarnation Therapy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T20:34:10-07:00","id":1403749,"title":"","content":"I mean, without resorting to straight up mind control..... He has political position that he's spent the last, like, 2000 years entrenching, allies that are with him on many more important issues than whether or not Solars need murdering, the Realm he helped build has &quot;Solars need murdering&quot; as a keystone of it's religion. <br /> <br /> Basically, I think it'd take a miracle. I mean that quite literally.<br /> <br /> As is, I would treat Chejop Kejak abandoning his position pretty much as an Unacceptable Order, barring him finding out something from an unimpeachable source that vastly changed his understanding of the universe....or being put up against something that exceeded the Godzilla Threshold by several orders of magnitude.<br /> <br /> So, to go with Aut's idea, find a way to have the friggen Maiden of Secrets show up to tell him about the Great Curse. And then, while he's still redecorating his mind about that, present him with some epic options for ending said curse so that Solars don't invariably go insane as they get older. And, while he's mulling that over, hit him with news of a Second Balorian War or the Deathlords and Abyssals marching forth upon Creation, or something similarly apocalyptic. You probably have to be far past the point where rallying the Entire Exalted Host is necessary to get him to admit it, but it would take something on that level to finally try to run with it, I think.<br /> <br /> Short of something that epically gonzo....I kinda doubt you could really do it. Chejop has had what he wanted for the last 700 years and change: a very stable Creation. If he can weather the next few years and actually get the Realm to have a proper way to deal with the line of succession without falling back into the Shogunate &quot;All the Wars, All the Time&quot; setup, then...basically, he'll have won. And he'll probably die shortly after too, but he's just... this.... close to winning forever before that happens.<br /> <br /> He's not gonna give that up easily. (Plus, again, basically his entire power base is intertwined with Solar Murdering, so it'll be even harder to give that up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T02:50:01-07:00","id":1403783,"title":"","content":"Instil actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T04:33:54-07:00","id":1405301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1403749#post1403749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short of something that epically gonzo....I kinda doubt you could really do it. Chejop has had what he wanted for the last 700 years and change: a very stable Creation. <b>If he can weather the next few years and actually get the Realm to have a proper way to deal with the line of succession without falling back into the Shogunate &quot;All the Wars, All the Time&quot; setup, then...basically, he'll have won.</b> And he'll probably die shortly after too, but he's just... this.... close to winning forever before that happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>How will this let him win? Forever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T05:04:28-07:00","id":1405307,"title":"","content":"I assume the point is that if the Realm survives the disappearance of the Empress, and manages to install a means of succession, it will stabilize for the forseeable future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T05:06:15-07:00","id":1405310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405307#post1405307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume the point is that if the Realm survives the disappearance of the Empress, and manages to install a means of succession, it will stabilize for the forseeable future.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's hundreds of extra solaroids coming out now from the woodwork. The Yozis now have their infernals, The Deathlords their Abyssals, and 150 Solar exaltations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T05:29:13-07:00","id":1405315,"title":"","content":"Maybe convince him that the Solars were framed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T07:57:00-07:00","id":1405337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405315#post1405315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe convince him that the Solars were framed?</div> </div> </div> </div>How? These were transcendent demigods capable of shaking heaven and earth. Who did it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T09:28:13-07:00","id":1405362,"title":"","content":"The Yozis. Specifically the Ebon Dragon. He\u2019s good at tricking people into believing things that aren\u2019t true. At least in 2e he got the Scarlet Empress to fall for him even though at the time he was the embodiment of Evil...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T09:44:06-07:00","id":1405368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405362#post1405362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yozis. Specifically the Ebon Dragon. He\u2019s good at tricking people into believing things that aren\u2019t true. At least in 2e he got the Scarlet Empress to fall for him even though at the time he was the embodiment of Evil...</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? How? What, did he whack Chejop Kejack with 'golden years tarnished black'? Did he do it for the dozens or so sidereal elders that were behind the Usurpation? Did he do it to the Dragonblooded host which smashed the Solar's shit in? As well as the Lunars who are witnesses to the horrors of the Deliberative itself? All of them? Without them noticing? Because these were monsters. Even the Dragonblooded hit essence 6/7 in those days. And that's not discounting perfect defenses. And holy effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T09:48:06-07:00","id":1405369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405362#post1405362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yozis. Specifically the Ebon Dragon. He\u2019s good at tricking people into believing things that aren\u2019t true. At least in 2e he got the Scarlet Empress to fall for him even though at the time he was the embodiment of Evil...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably a poor strategy in Ex3 since the Yozis there are not 2e's Yozis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T09:53:31-07:00","id":1405370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405369#post1405369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a poor strategy in Ex3 since the Yozis there are not 2e's Yozis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor 1Es. The Ebon Dragon being pure evil is basically now the exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:18:41-07:00","id":1405381,"title":"","content":"You don't and he's going to die in like five years anyway. Dude has spent thousands--<i>thousands</i> of years running the Realm and making sure it works. You don't just stop doing that.<br /> <br /> Also, let's be real here: it's hard to remember given that the Solars are the &quot;main character&quot; splat, but Kejak had completely legitimate reasons for the things he did. The Solars were <i>literally insane</i> tyrants ruining everything. There is zero proof they won't be again as far as he knows. People treat the Usurpation like the Sids and DB's just murdered innocent Solars (and therefore you can convince Kejak he was wrong). Kejak can just bring up a history of Awful Shit Solars Did to anyone trying to make him regret his decision.<br /> <br /> Which is why my Eclipse when he finally got to meet him didn't attack him or even blame him, he just said &quot;Thanks, <i>asshole</i>&quot;, and then bounced, lmao","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T12:51:40-07:00","id":1405400,"title":"","content":"He has had thousands of years to become set in his mindset, the only thing that seems likely to have a shot is an earlier posts suggestion of trying to get him to decide the new solars can be managed so that they don't grow into lunatics like the last batch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T16:12:53-07:00","id":1405413,"title":"","content":"No! You misunderstood me. I didn\u2019t mean the Solars were really framed. That would destroy the tragedy of the setting. I mean convince Chejop Kejak that the Ebon Dragon framed the Solars. He is a being of death and darkness. People are always willing to believe the worst of him.<br /> <br /> I read the 3e corebook and What Fire Has Wrought. There\u2019s like nothing at all in either of those about the individual Yozis. The Ebon Dragon would make the perfect bogeyman.<br /> <br /> Come on. Isn\u2019t the idea of framing somebody for framing somebody else kinda cool? \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T16:21:09-07:00","id":1405417,"title":"","content":"On second thought, it\u2019s unlikely someone who lived through the excesses and mad Solars of the First Age could be convinced the whole thing was faked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T16:30:25-07:00","id":1405418,"title":"","content":"I don't think you could convince him the reasons for the Great Prophecy were faked.<br /> Where you might be able to gain some leverage is if you can prove some of the Bronze Faction who voted in the Great Convention had been in service of an outside power that wished to weaken the Exalted Host such as the Yozis or Neverborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T16:55:46-07:00","id":1405419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405381#post1405381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't and he's going to die in like five years anyway. Dude has spent thousands--<i>thousands</i> of years running the Realm and making sure it works. You don't just stop doing that.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that along with &quot;Ebon Dragon is embodiement of Evil&quot;, &quot;Chejob will drop dead any minute&quot; was also a bit of a 2eism. In his first ficiton piece from 1e, he thought he still had a century or two to him.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T17:14:17-07:00","id":1405420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405381#post1405381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't and he's going to die in like five years anyway. Dude has spent thousands--<i>thousands</i> of years running the Realm and making sure it works. You don't just stop doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I recall <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Christmas_Carol\" target=\"_blank\">a certain other story</a> where an old man was due to die after a lifetime spent running an exploitative business. It admittedly took quite an ordeal for him to change his ways, but he <i>did</i> stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T17:34:01-07:00","id":1405426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405418#post1405418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you could convince him the reasons for the Great Prophecy were faked.<br /> Where you might be able to gain some leverage is if you can prove some of the Bronze Faction who voted in the Great Convention had been in service of an outside power that wished to weaken the Exalted Host such as the Yozis or Neverborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s kind of what I was thinking. But you put it in better words than I did. Do you think the Ebon Dragon specifically could\u2019ve been responsible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T17:35:13-07:00","id":1405427,"title":"","content":"I see the Ebon Dragon as the Demon Lover, the great seducer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T18:53:33-07:00","id":1405445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405426#post1405426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s kind of what I was thinking. But you put it in better words than I did. Do you think the Ebon Dragon specifically could\u2019ve been responsible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chejop didn't work alone. Besides, Sidereals have perfect defenses against mental attacks. An attack by the Ebon Dragon (how the hell does he do it from inside Malfeas?) would just be shrugged off, and its quite possible that Chejop would hit him with a Sidereal martial art to turn him inside out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T04:26:10-07:00","id":1405542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405381#post1405381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't and he's going to die in like five years anyway. Dude has spent thousands--<i>thousands</i> of years running the Realm and making sure it works. You don't just stop doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise of this thread is not that he just stops doing it.<br /> <br /> It is that he is convinced to stop by player characters.<br /> <br /> The most likely candidates of which are Solar player characters.<br /> <br /> The social prowess of Solars combined with being able to undermine his beliefs with positive examples that he has not possessed throughout those hundreds of years (definitely not even two thousand, so thousand singular plus change)? I should hope that there will not be Sidereal Charms that render him impervious to that. It's probably been easy enough to maintain the belief that Solars were rotten to the core when there were hardly any around to provide counter examples.<br /> <br /> Not a sure thing by any means, there are prejudices and old habits that a person can double down on through just about anything, and even Solars find a challenge to overcome. But the tools identifiably exist within system and setting, and ought to be recognised in such a discussion.<br /> <br /> The opening post regards it as a task more epic than one engaging the Neverborn, but I should think far from it. For though I speak it to you, I think Chejop is but a man, as I am. The violet smells to him as it doth to me, in his nakedness he appears but a man. Therefore, his fears, out of doubt, be of the same relish as ours are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T09:52:46-07:00","id":1405597,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> the Ebon Dragon is a godlike entity. More powerful than most gods and older than all of them. He probably could defeat even the oldest Sidereal regardless of what the rules say about \u201cperfect\u201d defenses. And even if he is trapped in Hell (which isn\u2019t called Malfeas anymore), he is certainly capable of indirectly manipulating events in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T13:23:11-07:00","id":1405659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405597#post1405597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> the Ebon Dragon is a godlike entity. More powerful than most gods and older than all of them. He probably could defeat even the oldest Sidereal regardless of what the rules say about \u201cperfect\u201d defenses. And even if he is trapped in Hell (which isn\u2019t called Malfeas anymore), he is certainly capable of indirectly manipulating events in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Still transcendent demigods. Primordials being able to power through perfect defenses makes the game invalid and lose coherence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T13:40:12-07:00","id":1405661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405426#post1405426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s kind of what I was thinking. But you put it in better words than I did. Do you think the Ebon Dragon specifically could\u2019ve been responsible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, he only really needs a sufficiently connected double agent at the Great Convention.<br /> <br /> He doesn't need to be the super-duper secret true architect of the Usurpation just someone who did enough to ensure it happened that if Chejop Kejak was confronted with evidence his faith in the plan might be shaken enough for Exalted social-fu to work its magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T14:32:35-07:00","id":1405666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405661#post1405661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, he only really needs a sufficiently connected double agent at the Great Convention.<br /> <br /> He doesn't need to be the super-duper secret true architect of the Usurpation just someone who did enough to ensure it happened that if Chejop Kejak was confronted with evidence his faith in the plan might be shaken enough for Exalted social-fu to work its magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. That makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T14:55:22-07:00","id":1405670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405597#post1405597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> the Ebon Dragon is a godlike entity. More powerful than most gods and older than all of them. He probably could defeat even the oldest Sidereal regardless of what the rules say about \u201cperfect\u201d defenses. And even if he is trapped in Hell (which isn\u2019t called Malfeas anymore), he is certainly capable of indirectly manipulating events in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game has always ran on a principle of Defense Always Wins. There's no trans-perfect special level of super-perfects that beat perfects. That kind of arms-racing is kidn of degenerate in many games and is something Exalted avoided. The Exalted defeated the enemies fo the gods with all the tools they ahve before Essence 5 basically. And part of that is there's no &quot;Better than perfect' effects in previous editions, and 3e in general voids such effects, but but also has nothing that circumvents the defenses we have.<br /> <br /> The game also doesn't give by default a presumption that ancientness or grandness give cart blanch immunity to other beings, nor to surpass their immunities. He's on the same playing field as everyone else, even if he has greater affordances on what he can do there. ANd part of that is he doesn't have some &quot;Screw over other characters perfectly&quot; power.<br /> <br /> Malfeas is also still synonnymous with Hell as a note. Hell just is often more used I think since it's easier to spell and folks tend to want to separate the location form the entity to speak on it broadly, but it never stopped beng Hell anymore than Yu-Shan stopped being Heaven.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T21:08:24-07:00","id":1405737,"title":"","content":"Are there any mental perfect defense in Ex3? If not then just convince Kejak with Social Action \u2018till he\u2019s dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T00:33:12-07:00","id":1405753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405737#post1405737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any mental perfect defense in Ex3? If not then just convince Kejak with Social Action \u2018till he\u2019s dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social influence doens't work quite like that, and generally berrating someone with a topic that goes pretty storng against one of their Defining intimacies is a good way for them to not listen to you to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T01:23:09-07:00","id":1405757,"title":"","content":"Yeah, having a bucket of success doesn\u2019t actually do much in the social game it seems when compare against combat.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m just mostly interested in the whole \u201cperfect mental defense\u201d angle since I remember one of the backer request something like that in the Miracle book but the author says no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T02:14:15-07:00","id":1405763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405670#post1405670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game has always ran on a principle of Defense Always Wins. There's no trans-perfect special level of super-perfects that beat perfects. That kind of arms-racing is kidn of degenerate in many games and is something Exalted avoided. The Exalted defeated the enemies fo the gods with all the tools they ahve before Essence 5 basically. And part of that is there's no &amp;quot;Better than perfect' effects in previous editions, and 3e in general voids such effects, but but also has nothing that circumvents the defenses we have.<br /> <br /> The game also doesn't give by default a presumption that ancientness or grandness give cart blanch immunity to other beings, nor to surpass their immunities. He's on the same playing field as everyone else, even if he has greater affordances on what he can do there. ANd part of that is he doesn't have some &amp;quot;Screw over other characters perfectly&amp;quot; power.<br /> <br /> Malfeas is also still synonnymous with Hell as a note. Hell just is often more used I think since it's easier to spell and folks tend to want to separate the location form the entity to speak on it broadly, but it never stopped beng Hell anymore than Yu-Shan stopped being Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Last paragraph) Okay, I didn\u2019t know that.<br /> <br /> I thought the Ebon Dragon was like an Antediluvian in Exalted. If he really wanted you dead you were pretty much dead, even if you were an elder Sidereal like Chejop Kejak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T05:23:31-07:00","id":1405780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405763#post1405763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Ebon Dragon was like an Antediluvian in Exalted. If he really wanted you dead you were pretty much dead, even if you were an elder Sidereal like Chejop Kejak.</div> </div> </div> </div>The beings who became the Yozis were able to be challenged and even defeated by the armies of the Exalted. While I wouldn't <i>bet on</i> a single Exalt who was facing off against one of those grand titans, at least one <i>did</i> manage to triumph over such an enemy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T06:55:50-07:00","id":1405785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405763#post1405763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Ebon Dragon was like an Antediluvian in Exalted. If he really wanted you dead you were pretty much dead, even if you were an elder Sidereal like Chejop Kejak.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ebon Dragon's main strength outside of a doomsday scenario is that he's basically an organisation capable of advancing his agenda through demons such as Alveua and Mara who are their own people with their own interests and connections within Creation but they're also to some extent a part of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:23:09-07:00","id":1405803,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> okay. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T15:08:41-07:00","id":1405840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405757#post1405757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m just mostly interested in the whole \u201cperfect mental defense\u201d angle since I remember one of the backer request something like that in the Miracle book but the author says no.</div> </div> </div> </div>3e does not have any omni-applicable &quot;perfect social defense&quot; charms, and I doubt it ever will. Solar Integrity has a number of effects that allow you to resist or totally reject influences that go against your core Intimacies, but nothing really that does the same if one of your core Intimacies is the one being leveraged to get you to agree. In 3e, Solar Integrity is about being true to yourself, upholding your key beliefs above all else, but that necessarily implies also being able to be persuaded based on those beliefs.<br /> <br /> More generally, perfect social defenses were, frankly, <i>boring</i> in 2e. A character with a lot of investment in Integrity could just go about saying &quot;nope!&quot; to every proposition, including totally reasonable offers that lined up with their stated ideologies. In my experience, it led to PCs where the player wasn't actually thinking about what the character wanted at all, just what would be the most tactically advantageous choice to make at all times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T18:04:48-07:00","id":1405861,"title":"","content":"Kejak is objectively one of the most intelligent and powerful beings in the known universe, maybe <i>the</i> most if we focus on humans. He doesn't <i>belong</i> to the Bronze faction. The Bronze faction exists because most Sidereals choose to align themselves with Kejak and his inner circle, and Kejak's considered (and popular!) opinion based on thousands of years of observation and a fair bit of foresight is that Solar-level power in falible human hands poses an existential risk to civilization and life as we know it.<br /> <br /> It may as well be physics, or statistics. Continuity needs stability, stability needs consistency. One massively powerful Solar is unpredictable and therefore dangerous. In a <i>society</i> of Dragon-blooded, on the other hand, individuals have less personal power and their impulses are tempered by their connections to each other.<br /> <br /> So what would it even mean for Kejak to &quot;switch factions&quot;? He'd have to decide that, like his protege Ayesha Ura professes, the benefits of controlling the relatively small number of powerful Solars outweigh the costs and the risks.<br /> <br /> Which, as it turns out, is either easy (if it's true) or impossible (if it's not). You'd need some challenge that Solars (as a group) could handle that no one else, even Sidereals backed by Heaven, cannot. In that case, the calculus changes.<br /> <br /> FWIW, in 3e, with its focus on Solars as individuals and on ground-level stories, I think the Bronze faction has a stronger case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T19:49:42-07:00","id":1405867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405861#post1405861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kejak is objectively one of the most intelligent and powerful beings in the known universe, maybe <i>the</i> most if we focus on humans. He doesn't <i>belong</i> to the Bronze faction. The Bronze faction exists because most Sidereals choose to align themselves with Kejak and his inner circle, and Kejak's considered (and popular!) opinion based on thousands of years of observation and a fair bit of foresight is that Solar-level power in falible human hands poses an existential risk to civilization and life as we know it.<br /> <br /> It may as well be physics, or statistics. Continuity needs stability, stability needs consistency. One massively powerful Solar is unpredictable and therefore dangerous. In a <i>society</i> of Dragon-blooded, on the other hand, individuals have less personal power and their impulses are tempered by their connections to each other.<br /> <br /> So what would it even mean for Kejak to &amp;quot;switch factions&amp;quot;? He'd have to decide that, like his protege Ayesha Ura professes, the benefits of controlling the relatively small number of powerful Solars outweigh the costs and the risks.<br /> <br /> Which, as it turns out, is either easy (if it's true) or impossible (if it's not). You'd need some challenge that Solars (as a group) could handle that no one else, even Sidereals backed by Heaven, cannot. In that case, the calculus changes.<br /> <br /> FWIW, in 3e, with its focus on Solars as individuals and on ground-level stories, I think the Bronze faction has a stronger case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Liked this post. Very intelligent and well-reasoned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T20:30:47-07:00","id":1405875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405763#post1405763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Last paragraph) Okay, I didn\u2019t know that.<br /> <br /> I thought the Ebon Dragon was like an Antediluvian in Exalted. If he really wanted you dead you were pretty much dead, even if you were an elder Sidereal like Chejop Kejak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted pretty purposefully avoids beings like the Antedeluvians. They can be challenged and in 2e he was even quite challengable. <i>Hard</i>, but doable by properly built PC groups in context of what properly built for 2e was.<br /> <br /> The fact that he's well, in Hell and never will get out by Exalted design, and surrendered due to his fear fod eath by the Exalted's hands, show he's quite defeatable. The Yozis are powerful, ancient, and vast beings. THey're still beings which operate in a setting where they are not just defeatable, but actually arelady defeated. And as Lioness notes, often in ways which don't look like giant kaiju rampages even if he himself looks a lot like one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T22:16:48-07:00","id":1405883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405861#post1405861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Kejak is objectively one of the most intelligent and powerful beings in the known universe, maybe <i>the</i> most if we focus on humans.</b> He doesn't <i>belong</i> to the Bronze faction. The Bronze faction exists because most Sidereals choose to align themselves with Kejak and his inner circle, and Kejak's considered (and popular!) opinion based on thousands of years of observation and a fair bit of foresight is that Solar-level power in falible human hands poses an existential risk to civilization and life as we know it.<br /> <br /> It may as well be physics, or statistics. Continuity needs stability, stability needs consistency. <b>One massively powerful Solar is unpredictable and therefore dangerous</b>. In a <i>society</i> of Dragon-blooded, on the other hand, individuals have less personal power and their impulses are tempered by their connections to each other.<br /> <br /> ... I think the Bronze faction has a stronger case</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna just let the bolded parts speak for itself, on why I find this hypocrisy annoying. Let alone that the power of the Dragonblooded is still being used on the powerless with little if no real consequences that I find the argument so weak.<br /> <br /> Still while Kejak is a old entrenched exalted, and honestly a interesting character. As others have stated it is possible if you wisely use the social system to do so. Although it may very well take a lot of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T03:34:37-07:00","id":1405910,"title":"","content":"I expect that Chejop can often benefit from the perfect social defence of being unlikely to be in the same room as a Solar, or anybody else that would strongly argue against his world view. That feels like it would be the biggest complicating factor; the system presents challenges to changing his mind, the story presents challenges to even being in the position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T05:24:54-07:00","id":1405918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405763#post1405763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Last paragraph) Okay, I didn\u2019t know that.<br /> <br /> I thought the Ebon Dragon was like an Antediluvian in Exalted. If he really wanted you dead you were pretty much dead, even if you were an elder Sidereal like Chejop Kejak.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the biggest differences of Exalted is that, no, you can't just get chumped by the big players. They always have to let the dice fall. And for the Ebon Dragon? He's already lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:04:06-07:00","id":1405922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405883#post1405883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna just let the bolded parts speak for itself, on why I find this hypocrisy annoying. Let alone that the power of the Dragonblooded is still being used on the powerless with little if no real consequences that I find the argument so weak.<br /> <br /> Still while Kejak is a old entrenched exalted, and honestly a interesting character. As others have stated it is possible if you wisely use the social system to do so. Although it may very well take a lot of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhhhh<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t read it that closely. I see your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T07:52:16-07:00","id":1405942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405883#post1405883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna just let the bolded parts speak for itself, on why I find this hypocrisy annoying. Let alone that the power of the Dragonblooded is still being used on the powerless with little if no real consequences that I find the argument so weak.<br /> <br /> Still while Kejak is a old entrenched exalted, and honestly a interesting character. As others have stated it is possible if you wisely use the social system to do so. Although it may very well take a lot of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a little &quot;it's okay if it's me&quot; deliberate hypocracy in there! But in Kejak's defense, Sidereals never get as powerful, or do so as quickly, as Solars can. Thousands of years later, even Kejak doesn't have anything like the personal power of elder Solars in their heyday. There are also fewer Sidereals, and they answer to Heaven's laws and Fate itself. Even a rogue Sidereal can only do so much harm.<br /> <br /> If you add to that the fact that Sidereals can literally see the impact of choices on the future, that their upbringing largely separates them from Earthly squables, that Arcane Fate hinders them from accumulating power and influence, and that their express mandate is &quot;the greater good of the world&quot;, Kejak's position doesn't seem so hypocritical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T08:56:29-07:00","id":1405952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405942#post1405942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a little &quot;it's okay if it's me&quot; deliberate hypocracy in there! But in Kejak's defense, Sidereals never get as powerful, or do so as quickly, as Solars can. Thousands of years later, even Kejak doesn't have anything like the personal power of elder Solars in their heyday. There are also fewer Sidereals, and they answer to Heaven's laws and Fate itself. Even a rogue Sidereal can only do so much harm.<br /> <br /> If you add to that the fact that Sidereals can literally see the impact of choices on the future, that their upbringing largely separates them from Earthly squables, that Arcane Fate hinders them from accumulating power and influence, and that their express mandate is &quot;the greater good of the world&quot;, Kejak's position doesn't seem so hypocritical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that this is 3e and not 1e or 2e. I find this line of thought really hard to justify myself. Celestial Exalted on a personnel level are too close to each other in power to for that line of thinking to be very effective. Also this is kinda ignoring the fact that a single Dragonblooded controls a weapon that if misused could destroy Creation itself.<br /> <br /> As for the second and slightly better point, while all of those cases are true, I also think it isn't necessarily a good thing that they are largely separated from the worst consequences of their actions and that Arcane Fate makes it hard to form attachments to Creation itself the thing that they are entrusted to help. This doesn't even mean that Sidereals <b>can't </b>be largely working selfishly for their own benefit in the context of Yu-Shan, which ultimately does effect Creation as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T10:08:47-07:00","id":1405957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405942#post1405942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a little &quot;it's okay if it's me&quot; deliberate hypocracy in there! But in Kejak's defense, Sidereals never get as powerful, or do so as quickly, as Solars can. Thousands of years later, even Kejak doesn't have anything like the personal power of elder Solars in their heyday. There are also fewer Sidereals, and they answer to Heaven's laws and Fate itself. Even a rogue Sidereal can only do so much harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say that a Sidereals book written in the same manner as our current Dragon-Blooded and Lunars books will talk about these Exalted less in the broad and in the abstract and more focused with examples of time, place and personalities. That also ought to mean that they've made contributions to the Age of Sorrows, for better and for worse (ultimately leaning a bit more into worse, because Time of Tumult), particularly since the setup with Sidereals makes them less visible when talking about the setting from other perspectives, so it has a lot of heavy lifting to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you add to that the fact that Sidereals can literally see the impact of choices on the future, that their upbringing largely separates them from Earthly squables, that Arcane Fate hinders them from accumulating power and influence, and that their express mandate is &quot;the greater good of the world&quot;, Kejak's position doesn't seem so hypocritical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this is a sentiment that leans very much in a direction of &quot;Sidereals primarily make good decisions&quot;, which I don't think is consistent with the game nor necessarily good for it. It's certainly fine for many of them to be trying to make the best decisions that they can, but... for a start, answering to Heaven's laws would seem to presume a benevolence or intelligence to Heaven that has never really been how it's characterised and is unlikely to start here. Sure they generally want to do things for the greater good of the world... as best they understand it, within their own conceptions and according to their own biases, and not necessarily the types to walk back and admit fault on a decision that went sour. Being uninvolved with the world's cultures... I say the best approach to that would be that it's the ideal, and certainly they don't have the kind of obvious temporal power that many Lunars and Terrestrials do, but it gets mixed up a bit with Sidereals who play favourites in the course of them going about their business and their private lives. The idea that Sidereals spend decent lengths of time off work promoting things in accordance with personal interests has always been part of the game, I think it could use more emphasis.<br /> <br /> Again, actual character examples will help these things to stick in a way that abstract description seems not to.<br /> <br /> If Chejop is much like he has been before, and from the core chapter fiction I expect the intention is that he has been, I'd say that in his own person he's not anything like the most terrible and conceited Solars, daimyos and Dynasts have been, but he still promotes and maintains the Realm and calls it a good job. Chejop does not profit off of what he's built, and arguably has never really had much in the way of peace from it. He's still ultimately propping the world up with an edifice that inflicts a lot of harm and justifies that with insistence that it's the best that could be done.<br /> <br /> I personally would not say that makes him a hypocrite; he's quite unlike the Solars that he overthrew or the Dragon Blooded whom he keeps on top. It just makes him dumb and wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T10:16:19-07:00","id":1405958,"title":"","content":"Re; Blackwell's response, I don't think it's wrong, but my perception of the Bronze stance is a bit less driven by a rational ideology, and more by...<br /> <br /> They did this prophecy a long time ago, by methods that to some degree work by irrational means, intuition, ritual and association, and it told them what happen. They had good rational reasons too, to believe that the result was true (an escalating pattern), and they had good evidence (past successes) that their methods generally worked! So they implemented the decision (perhaps with some personal difficulty, perhaps without much, depending on who they were as individuals).<br /> <br /> Since then, they've been juggling from crisis-to-crisis. And they're in fixed relationships with a bunch of stakeholders like the Dragonblooded and certain of the gods who don't want them to come to a different result, and they can't easily pivot to supporting the Solar Exalted - since burying the hatchet is hard when the other party wants to bury it in your head. And it seems likely none of their more recents attempts of prediction, albeit conducted at a smaller scale, have yielded much more insight strongly one way or the other (&quot;If the Solars returned then...&quot; - I absolutely refuse to believe the Sidereals have never asked the question again!).<br /> <br /> Basically I guess I'm saying that from my perception, Chejop Kejak trusts less in his intelligence and ideology, and more in his prophetic powers and intuition, and those prophetic powers and intuition have never given him enough of an indication that another choice would be better (then or now), not enough to mitigate the serious complications that it would present to what he sees as his immediate tasks. So to some extent, convincing him is not, probably so much a matter of *just* dropping in and making some sufficiently clever argument using Solar debate powers that demolishes an ideological stance; why he believes what he does rides on some experiences and means of getting information that you don't really have too much access to, and on circumstances of the world that must be changed before his response to them will change.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that if you were to convince him at all, you convince him by being heroes and doing the deeds such that heroes do, and by making the kind of world where its safer for him to bet on you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T11:06:56-07:00","id":1405967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403729-how-can-you-make-chejop-kejak-turn-gold-faction?p=1405957#post1405957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to say that a Sidereals book written in the same manner as our current Dragon-Blooded and Lunars books will talk about these Exalted less in the broad and in the abstract and more focused with examples of time, place and personalities. That also ought to mean that they've made contributions to the Age of Sorrows, for better and for worse (ultimately leaning a bit more into worse, because Time of Tumult), particularly since the setup with Sidereals makes them less visible when talking about the setting from other perspectives, so it has a lot of heavy lifting to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel as though this is a sentiment that leans very much in a direction of &amp;quot;Sidereals primarily make good decisions&amp;quot;, which I don't think is consistent with the game nor necessarily good for it. It's certainly fine for many of them to be trying to make the best decisions that they can, but... for a start, answering to Heaven's laws would seem to presume a benevolence or intelligence to Heaven that has never really been how it's characterised and is unlikely to start here. Sure they generally want to do things for the greater good of the world... as best they understand it, within their own conceptions and according to their own biases, and not necessarily the types to walk back and admit fault on a decision that went sour. Being uninvolved with the world's cultures... I say the best approach to that would be that it's the ideal, and certainly they don't have the kind of obvious temporal power that many Lunars and Terrestrials do, but it gets mixed up a bit with Sidereals who play favourites in the course of them going about their business and their private lives. The idea that Sidereals spend decent lengths of time off work promoting things in accordance with personal interests has always been part of the game, I think it could use more emphasis.<br /> <br /> Again, actual character examples will help these things to stick in a way that abstract description seems not to.<br /> <br /> If Chejop is much like he has been before, and from the core chapter fiction I expect the intention is that he has been, I'd say that in his own person he's not anything like the most terrible and conceited Solars, daimyos and Dynasts have been, but he still promotes and maintains the Realm and calls it a good job. Chejop does not profit off of what he's built, and arguably has never really had much in the way of peace from it. He's still ultimately propping the world up with an edifice that inflicts a lot of harm and justifies that with insistence that it's the best that could be done.<br /> <br /> I personally would not say that makes him a hypocrite; he's quite unlike the Solars that he overthrew or the Dragon Blooded whom he keeps on top. It just makes him dumb and wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the Sidereals, and I wouldn\u2019t mind playing a Chosen of Venus, so I\u2019m definitely looking forward to a Sidereals book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T09:33:56-07:00","id":1407963,"title":"","content":"Kill Kejak.<br /> Now free of the Great Curse, Kejak's ghost will realize what he has done.<br /> Kejak's ghost now haunts the Sidereals, trying to fix everything he did wrong.<br /> ??? - A really really confused Five Score Fellowship.<br /> Profit? Confusion? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}